                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I absolutely love the whole Lacey's flash games series, so it hurts a lot to give this game a thumbs down. It's just not worth $25, hell its not even worth 15$. Even before playing, the game had a very rough launch. It got delayed literally last second on the 27th, and the devs didn't make an announcement until an hour after it was supposed to release saying there were some \"administrative issues\". Then it got rescheduled to the 31st. No specific time given for release so that messed with mine and a lot of peoples Halloween plans, and we also didn't even get the price until the game had launched. A lot of the negativity towards the game was because of the lack of communication from the devs, and their habit of only announcing things after they already happened.\n\nNow talking about the game itself. I was hoping for a lot more mystery and actual arg style work, but finding the \"secrets\" of the games mainly comes from waiting for a timer to run out or doing something very obviously wrong which is just boring. The only time I felt like I actually did something myself was during the petshop minigame. So the gameplay is a little boring, but it's whatever. At least the story is interesting, right? Well idk cause on top of everything else the game was also BUGGED. For like the first 3 hours of release the entire community was stuck on the part right after the diner break, and there was literally no way to progress.\n\nthe very rocky launch, an absurd price tag of $25, and releasing in a broken state all just kinda killed my interest to play through the game further. It really sucks too cause I was SUPER hype for this game, I've been following it since it appeared on steam and I'm pretty sure I was one of the very first people to buy it. I really wanted to like this game, but everything I've mentioned just kinda made wanna get my money back rather than see it through. I'll prolly just watch some youtuber play it, and I recommend you do the same whoever is reading this.\n\nEdit: the bug blocking progress is fixed it but looks like people are running into MORE issues, as if that wasn't bad enough. Super glad I refunded now.\n\nEdit 2: Just watched a youtuber play it and now I'm SUPER SUPER glad I refunded, gameplay was the equivalent of a frustrating walking sim.",
